## Handoff Brief — Stage 8 hardening: automate the edge sweep
Branch `chore/sprint-2-polish` is checked out in /home/user/Web-Calculator-fresh (don't switch; the ux-ui-designer is editing docs/process/ui-design.md, mockup.html and screenshots in parallel — touch only tests/).
- Objective: add `sabee-khan-calculator/tests/e2e/edge.spec.ts` (IDs E-EDGE.1…) so the CLAUDE.md §12 edge sweep runs on all 3 engines in CI. Use the existing fixtures (console guard). Cover, asserting exact catalogue texts from src/messages.ts / docs/user-stories.md and A-12..A-18:
  - whitespace-only in each field → idle prompt/no error; lone "." → treated as empty (A-18); lone "-" and "-." → negative message;
  - very long input (400 digits) in each field → correct error, no NaN/Infinity/undefined, no horizontal scroll;
  - pasted values via clipboard-free `fill` and via `page.keyboard.insertText`: " 17.5 ", "$17", "17,5", "1e400", "+5", "007" (accepted as 7);
  - repeated Enter (×5) changes nothing; page reload → idle with pass mark "70";
  - every state's visible text never contains "NaN", "Infinity", "undefined"; result area never blank;
  - key-by-key typing of "17.5" and ".5" never flashes an error mid-number.
- Don't duplicate assertions already in S-1..S-3 specs more than needed. If any case fails, STOP and report it as a defect (do not change src/).
- Run `npx playwright test --project=chromium` (all specs green, no console errors) and `npm test`. Commit on the branch: `test(sprint-2): automate the edge sweep (E-EDGE.x)` with trailers `Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>` and `Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KhFfG85wfAdyRSPyKLHfUW`. Only add that one file to the commit (`git add sabee-khan-calculator/tests/e2e/edge.spec.ts`) — other agents have uncommitted doc changes in the tree. Do NOT push.
